{
    "background_story": "Luna grew up in a small village where access to clean water was a daily struggle. As a child, she would often watch as her mother and other women trekked for miles to fetch water from a distant well. One day, a team of engineers arrived to install a new standpipe in the village center. Luna was fascinated by the tall, metal pipe that brought water right to their doorstep. She became fast friends with the lead engineer, who taught her about the mechanics of the standpipe and the importance of proper maintenance. As she grew older, Luna took it upon herself to ensure the standpipe was always in good working order, earning her the nickname 'Guardian of the Standpipe.' Her dedication brought her community together, and soon the village was thriving. Luna's connection to the standpipe had sparked a sense of purpose and pride in her community.",
